# DI-first (pyiv)

Default path is **pyiv**. New services, backends, harness families, and CLI/API
wiring go through `MechaHarnessConfig` and constructor injection. Do not add
string registries, service locators, or a global injector.

Extend by **subclassing Config**. Override `get_inference_class()` /
`get_harness_class()` (and maps like `inference_classes()`). Host apps subclass
`MechaHarnessConfig` and call `super().configure()`.

Constructors take types pyiv can inject (`InferenceStrategy`, `Settings`,
`HarnessConfig`, `ToolRegistry`), not `str`/`dict` bags the injector cannot resolve.

OpenAPI is the **non-DI facade**, not a second architecture. `RunRequest` / `run()`
may hide the injector; they must still construct a Config and inject. Do not grow
`factory.py` back into a registry.

Only `mechaharness.di` and `mechaharness.factory.run` import pyiv. Domain types
stay injector-agnostic so host apps can inject them.

```python
# BAD — new global registry
register_inference("my_backend")(factory)

# GOOD — Config hook
class MyConfig(MechaHarnessConfig):
    def get_inference_class(self):
        return MyStrategy
```
